## What was built

A working **NFCorpus Live Retrieval Diagnostics Workbench** in `/Users/lily/dev/pi-bench/anserini-nfcorpus/claude-workspace/`.

### Files

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Dockerfile` | `eclipse-temurin:21-jdk` + Python; downloads `anserini-${ANSERINI_VERSION}-fatjar.jar` from Maven Central per the `install-anserini-fatjar` skill |
| `entrypoint.sh` | Binds `0.0.0.0:$PORT` (default `10000`), uses `/data` cache dir |
| `render.yaml` | Render Blueprint: docker runtime, `/health` check, 1 GB disk at `/data` |
| `app/anserini.py` | Subprocess wrappers for `PrebuiltIndexRegistry`, `ReproduceFromPrebuiltIndexes --show/--dry-run`, `SearchCollection`, `TrecEval` (real commands, no mocks) |
| `app/restserver.py` | Manages `io.anserini.api.RestServer` lifecycle on internal port `8081` |
| `app/setup.py` | Background pipeline: Java check → fatjar verify → reproduction discovery → SearchCollection → TrecEval → compare observed vs expected |
| `app/server.py` | Flask app with `/health`, `/api/status`, `/api/search`, `/api/evaluation`, `/api/evaluation/rerun`, `/api/artifacts`, `/api/artifact-preview` |
| `app/static/{index.html,app.js,styles.css}` | Dashboard with readiness, search, evaluation (observed vs expected with deltas), commands drawer, deployment contract panel |
| `tests/test_e2e.py` | Playwright + API test that fails on mocked output |
| `README.md` | Docker/Render run instructions, API table, troubleshooting |

### Verified locally (Python 3.13)

- `/health` reaches `phase=ready` in ~30 s on a warm cache
- `/api/search?q=diabetes diet` returns real BM25 hits with docids, scores, titles, and 1.5 KB document text per result (via `io.anserini.api.RestServer`)
- `/api/evaluation` reports observed `ndcg_cut_10 = 0.3218` matching expected `nDCG@10 = 0.3218` discovered from `ReproduceFromPrebuiltIndexes --config beir.core --show` → `status: match, delta: 0.0`
- `/api/evaluation/rerun` re-executes both commands and bumps the rerun counter
- Playwright test passes: **2 passed in 6.02s**

### PRD compliance highlights

- Skills consumed in order: `install-anserini-fatjar` (Dockerfile + jar verification), `anserini-cli` (`PrebuiltIndexRegistry`, `RestServer`, `Search`), `anserini-reproduction` (`ReproduceFromPrebuiltIndexes --show/--dry-run` for target discovery)
- Only NFCorpus is downloaded (~7 MB prebuilt index); no whole-BEIR or MS MARCO downloads
- Live search is backed by `io.anserini.api.RestServer`, not a custom search implementation
- Search results include rank, docid, score, title, and full document text from the prebuilt index
- All Anserini commands (verify, discover, search, eval, RestServer) are surfaced in the UI with exit code, elapsed time, stdout, stderr
- Expected metric is *discovered* from the reproduction YAML, not hardcoded
- Render contract: `0.0.0.0:$PORT` (default 10000), `/health` with all required fields, `/data` mount point documented, no interactive setup
- E2E test asserts numeric observed and expected values, a real delta/status, real document content, and that the rerun endpoint actually re-executes Anserini